Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] Occlusion culling: point lights hidden behind walls left out

With [Camera] occlusion light culling on, the scene camera's lights in view space leave out the point lights whose
sphere of influence is hidden everywhere behind the occlusion buffer's occluders (the support library's
occlusionLightOccluded): they light no pixel that is drawn, and each object's light list, and so its shader's light
loop, is shorter. Off, or for other cameras, the call returns false.
---
 components/sceneutil/lightmanager.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/components/sceneutil/lightmanager.cpp b/components/sceneutil/lightmanager.cpp
index a675d575a2..986de7abf3 100644
--- a/components/sceneutil/lightmanager.cpp
+++ b/components/sceneutil/lightmanager.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 
 #include <osgUtil/CullVisitor>
 
+#include <alpha3/upstream.hpp>
 #include <components/debug/debuglog.hpp>
 #include <components/misc/constants.hpp>
 #include <components/resource/scenemanager.hpp>
@@ -599,6 +600,10 @@ namespace SceneUtil
                     transform.mLightSource->setLastAppliedFrame(frameNum);
                 }
 
+                // hidden behind walls, it lights nothing that is drawn
+                if (Alpha3::occlusionLightOccluded(*cv, viewBound))
+                    continue;
+
                 LightSourceViewBound l;
                 l.mLightSource = transform.mLightSource;
                 l.mViewBound = viewBound;
